---
title: XState alpha.69 migration
summary: Exact pins, upstream compatibility checks, and the source mirror choice.
---

# XState alpha.69 migration

This page started at `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.69` and `@xstate/effect@1.0.0-alpha.8`.
The current pins are `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.71` and `@xstate/effect@1.0.0-alpha.10`; see the alpha.71 section.
Effect stays at `4.0.0`. The bridge peers accept Effect `^4.0.0` and XState `^6.0.0-alpha.68`.

## Upstream changes

- [Alpha.66](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.66) fixes entry, exit, and declaration inference.
- [Alpha.67 changelog](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/blob/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.69/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md#600-alpha67) renames executable action types and freezes plain context objects in development. State inputs leave with their states.
- [Alpha.68](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.68) renames public APIs and built-in events. Actor references serialize as `{ $actor: address }`. Persisted timers become lists.
- [Alpha.69](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.69) fixes literal output inference in `createAsyncLogic`.
- [Bridge alpha.8](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/%40xstate/effect%401.0.0-alpha.8) replaces the three `fromEffect*` constructors with `createEffect*Logic` constructors.

## Repository impact

- Rename declared Effect logic in core, deploy, flags, learn, and the learning card.
- Keep `Stream.fromEffect` in request incidents. It belongs to Effect, not the bridge.
- Update `xstate-effect/no-inline-effect` for all three constructors. Real Oxlint fixtures cover each inline spawn and the declared alternative.
- `rat-stack-patterns/watch-effect-actors` already checks `createEffectActor`. That name does not change.
- No runtime code imports the removed core APIs or executable action types.
- No runtime code restores XState snapshots or reads timer records, actor-reference envelopes, or state inputs.
- Existing model and lifecycle tests exercise completion, failure, retry, and scoped actor execution. The inspection model uses category events with `actorId` already.

## Source mirror

The bridge release tag contains core alpha.68. The core alpha.69 tag contains bridge alpha.8.
The bridge directory has no diff between these two tags.

For alpha.69, the mirror script selected `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.69` and checked both package versions.
It also requires the exact bridge release tag to exist.
This keeps source-first work aligned with both installed pins.

## Follow-up

The alpha.69 packet deferred the peers refresh. The alpha.70 gardener pass completes that refresh.
Apps that copy rat-stack must update both pins, rename bridge constructors, and audit persisted snapshots before restoring them.
Old actor-reference and timer formats are not accepted by alpha.68 and later.

## Alpha.70 and bridge alpha.9

The 2026-10-20 update pins `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.70` and `@xstate/effect@1.0.0-alpha.9` together.
Effect stays at `4.0.0`. The bridge peers require Effect `^4.0.0` and XState `^6.0.0-alpha.70`.

- [Core changelog](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/blob/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.70/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md#600-alpha70) removes `ActorRefFromLogic` and narrows `ActorRefFrom` to logic types.
- State ids change. Hash targets resolve whole ids. Implicit invoke ids use `<stateId>:<index>`.
- State keys require escaped dots. Bare string transitions throw. Versioned machines require an explicit id.
- Invoked actors with required input now require an input mapper. Graph traversal requires samples for events with payloads.
- Inline invokes no longer persist synthetic source names. Consumers with stored snapshots must migrate old ids and synthetic sources.
- [Bridge changelog](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/blob/%40xstate/effect%401.0.0-alpha.9/packages/xstate-effect/CHANGELOG.md#100-alpha9) changes root parallel tags to the machine id, or an empty string without an id.

Our machines need no call-site changes. They already use declared logic, object transitions, and required invoke inputs.
The inspection graph test supplies both completion payloads. Runtime code uses no removed type helpers, tagged states, or persisted XState snapshots.
The three `createEffect*Logic` constructors keep their names. The inline-Effect lint rule and its real Oxlint fixtures remain unchanged.

The core alpha.70 and bridge alpha.9 tags contain identical core and bridge trees.
The source mirror selects the core tag and verifies both package versions.
Registry checks confirm SHA-512 tarball integrity and GitHub Actions provenance for both packages.
Neither tarball declares lifecycle scripts or runtime dependencies. The age exceptions remain exact versions.

Consumers must move both pins, refresh mirrors, and run their lifecycle tests.
Audit persisted snapshots, whole-id targets, graph payload samples, and root parallel tag matching before upgrading.

## Alpha.71 and bridge alpha.10

The update moves both exact npm pins together. Effect stays at `4.0.7`.
The bridge peers accept XState `^6.0.0-alpha.71`, Effect `^4.0.0`, and optional `@oxlint/plugins` `^1.76.0`; our lint plugin runtime is `1.88.0`.

- [Core release](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/xstate%406.0.0-alpha.71) adds system-wide emission observation and improves graph traversal, serialization diagnostics, and invalid-snapshot errors.
- [Bridge release](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/releases/tag/%40xstate%2Feffect%401.0.0-alpha.10) carries complete Effect Causes in `EffectFailure<E>`. Invoked child `onError` handlers read `event.error.cause`. `join` replays the original Cause, including defects and interruption.
- Inspection, learning-log commit, and feedback-device machines retain the Cause and lift it with `Effect.failCause`. Public capability failures stay unchanged. The inspection machine's exported `Unreadable` outcome now carries `cause`, not a bare `error`.
- Existing `join(...).pipe(Effect.orDie)` boundaries remain deliberate: machine-level failures are defects there, while expected domain failures travel through final output. `watchActor` and the devtools watcher read status, context, and opaque events, not domain fields on snapshot errors; no watcher migration is needed.
- The compiled `@xstate/effect/oxlint` rule replaces our copy. Both implementations have the same constructor set, enqueue names, return traversal, Promise wrapper handling, and diagnostics. Upstream fixtures and our real-Oxlint fixtures cover discarded actions and inline spawns. Severity stays `error`.
- `sendAndAwait` replaces the inspection model test's send-plus-yield mailbox guess. `createSnapshotCodec` is deferred because runtime code does not persist XState snapshots.

The source mirror uses `xstate@6.0.0-alpha.71`; both release tags resolve to the same commit and match both package versions. Exact release-age exclusions move in place. Historical peer observations above retain their original versions.

Consumers must move both pins, preserve Causes in invoked-child error handling, wrap synthetic Effect errors with `EffectFailure`, and rerun lifecycle tests. Do not turn defects or interruption into expected domain errors.
